# SCSS Styling Standards

## CSS/HTML Styling Standards
- **Strictly use BEM (Block Element Modifier) convention for all CSS classes**
- Block: `.card`, `.header`, `.navigation`
- Element: `.card__title`, `.header__logo`, `.navigation__item`
- Modifier: `.card--featured`, `.header--fixed`, `.navigation__item--active`
- Never use nested selectors beyond BEM structure
- Avoid generic class names like `.red`, `.big`, `.left`
- Use semantic class names that describe purpose, not appearance
- Keep BEM blocks independent and reusable
- Use single hyphens for multi-word blocks: `.search-form`, `.user-profile`
- Ensure all HTML elements have proper BEM class names, avoid styling by tag names
- For comments use "//" instead of "/* */"

## File Organization
```scss
// Order of placement in .scss files:
// 1. Imports
@import 'variables';
@import 'mixins';

// 2. Variables
$label-width: 30%;
--text-color: #333;

// 3. Component styles
.component-name {
  // styles
}

```

## Nesting and Structure
- Use SCSS nesting effectively, avoid deep nesting (max 3 levels)
- Each component should have main container class matching filename

```scss
// Good nesting structure
.form-canvas {
  .canvas-heading {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    
    .canvas-title {
      font-weight: bold;
    }
  }
  
  .canvas-content {
    padding: 1rem;
  }
}

// Avoid flat CSS in SCSS
.form-group .form-control { border-radius: 0px; }
.form-group .form-label { padding: 0px; }

// Use SCSS nesting instead
.form-group {
  .form-control {
    border-radius: 0px;
  }
  
  .form-label {
    padding: 0px;
  }
}
```

## CSS Class Naming
- Use kebab-case: `user-profile`, `submit-btn`, `form-control-settings`
- Be descriptive, avoid generic names: Use `primary-action-btn` not `orange-txt`
- Follow BEM convention where appropriate
- Maintain consistency across components

## Component-Specific Styling
- Each component must have styles scoped to main container
- Avoid global style pollution
- Use CSS custom properties for theming support
